    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change implementing soft-delete for owners.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Soft-delete on DELETE** \u2014 `DeleteOwner.java` now sets `deleted = true` and `save()`s the owner instead of removing the row. `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` still returns 204 (2xx) via the unchanged `RespondWithNoContent` step.\n\n**New `deleted` field** on the `Owner` entity (`Owner.java`), defaulting to `Boolean.FALSE` \u2014 so a freshly created owner (built via the mapper, no DB round-trip) is `deleted: false`. Added:\n- The `deleted` column to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) with `DEFAULT FALSE`. Tests use the hsqldb schema (`ddl-auto=none`), so that column is what makes persistence work.\n- The `deleted` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema in `openapi.yml`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it \u2014 `GET` now returns `deleted`.\n\n**Create checks ignore deleted owners:**\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 the blocking household-duplicate check now skips owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n- `AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 the soft-duplicate flag likewise ignores deleted owners.\n\n## Verification\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass, and the full suite is green:\n- `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` \u2014 created owner reads `deleted:false`; after DELETE the record is retained and GET returns `deleted:true`.\n- `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` \u2014 recreating a soft-deleted owner's identical payload now succeeds (2xx).\n\n```\nTests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```",
